<title>HONG KONG: Peregrine awarded US$4.1 mln damages.</title>
<headline>Peregrine awarded US$4.1 mln damages.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peregrine Investments Holdings Ltd said on Thursday it had been awarded damages of US$4.1 million by a New York district court which rendered judgement against a former chairman of Peregrine's Burma subsidiary.</p>
<p>The company's lawsuit against Miriam Marshall Segal was based on her breach of fiduciary duties as well as the terms of her employment contract, Peregrine said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
